# Release, handoff, and README SOP (Ledgerly ERP)

When the user asks for a **shipping build**, **release**, **hotfix binaries**, **SOP completion**, or finishing work that affects **downloadable installers** or **README download docs**, do **all** that apply—**without waiting to be reminded**.

## Git (when code or README download docs change)

1. `git status` — no unintended files.
2. Commit with a clear message (why / what).
3. `git push` to the user’s branch (usually `main`). Diagnose push failures; do not end with “you should push.”

## Builds

1. `dotnet build` Shared → Server → Client **`-c Release`**.
2. When packaging installers: use `build_installers.ps1` / `installer/ledgerly.iss` **if** that pipeline matches the current C# outputs; otherwise publish/copy Release binaries and compile Inno Setup so assets exist before uploading.
3. Expected release asset names (update README if names change):
   - `LedgerlySetup.exe` — combined (Client and/or Server)
   - `LedgerlyClientSetup.exe` — client only
   - `LedgerlyServerSetup.exe` — server only

## README Downloads (required for a new Release)

1. Update **`README.md` → Downloads** with **verbatim** HTTPS links:
   `https://github.com/devildog5x5/ERP/releases/download/{tag}/{asset}`
2. Keep the table rows for **Combined**, **Client only**, and **Server only** honest — if an asset is only on an older tag, link that tag; do not imply an old installer is the newest code.
3. Refresh latest-release notes (tag links, default login `admin`/`admin`, API `http://127.0.0.1:8000`).
4. **Never invent** working `releases/download/...` URLs. Use `gh release view {tag} --json assets` after upload.
5. Commit and push the README with the release.

## Chat handoff — **### New build links** (every rebuild / release)

| Line | Content |
|------|---------|
| **Combined** | Full URL to `LedgerlySetup.exe` (or Local path if not uploaded) |
| **Client** | Full URL to `LedgerlyClientSetup.exe` (or Local path) |
| **Server** | Full URL to `LedgerlyServerSetup.exe` (or Local path) |
| **Release page** | `https://github.com/devildog5x5/ERP/releases/tag/{tag}` |
| **Local smoke** | Full paths to `Ledgerly.Server.exe` and `Ledgerly.Client.exe` when built locally |

Do **not** end with “see README” as the only download hint.

## Limits

- Creating tags / uploading release assets needs `gh` auth. If upload fails: still build locally, update README as pending if needed, push commits, and give **exact filenames** + intended URLs for the user to finish upload.
